,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4070.698881958,"data":"       | Thus we can count residues from the set S = {x mod (b-1) such that for each prime power factor p_i^{e_i} of b-1, x ≡ 0 or 1 (mod p_i^{e_i})}. Among these residues, we need those in the range [L, b-1] where L = ceil(sqrt(b)). Since residues are in [0, b-2] plus also residue 0 corresponds to s = b-1 (since we also consider s = b-1). So we need to count s values in [L, b-1] that are congruent to a solution residue.\n"}
