,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4070.700461395,"data":"       | Thus s^2 ∈ [b, b^2 - 1] =\u003e sqrt(b) ≤ s ≤ sqrt(b^2 - 1) = b - epsilon. So s must be integer between ceil(sqrt(b)) and b-1 (since s \u003c b). Indeed s ≤ b-1 because s^2 \u003c b^2, so s ≤ b-1. Also s ≥ ceil(sqrt(b)). Since b≥2, sqrt(b) \u003c b for b\u003e1.\n"}
