,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799032556,"data":"       | analysisWe need to find number of nonnegative integer triples (a,b,c) satisfying sum=300 and symmetric sum of pairwise terms a^2 b + a^2 c + b^2 a + b^2 c + c^2 a + c^2 b = 6,000,000.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.79903544,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799036937,"data":"       | We can rewrite expression: sum_{sym} a^2 b = sum_{cyc} a^2 b + a b^2? Wait sym sum includes both a^2 b and a b^2 for each unordered pair. Actually expression includes a^2 b + a^2 c + b^2 a + b^2 c + c^2 a + c^2 b = sum_{i≠j} a_i^2 a_j = sum_{i} a_i^2 (sum_{j≠i} a_j) = sum_i a_i^2 (S - a_i) where S = a+b+c = 300.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799039832,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799040939,"data":"       | Thus expression = Σ a_i^2 (S - a_i) = Σ (S a_i^2 - a_i^3) = S Σ a_i^2 - Σ a_i^3.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799042642,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799043852,"data":"       | Given S=300, we have 300 Σ a_i^2 - Σ a_i^3 = 6,000,000.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.79904515,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799046259,"data":"       | Thus Σ a_i^3 = 300 Σ a_i^2 - 6,000,000.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799047494,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799048707,"data":"       | We also have Σ a_i = 300.\n"}
