,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799103451,"data":"       | analysisSo (a+b)(b+c)(c+a) = Σ a^2 b + Σ a b^2 + 2abc. But Σ a^2 b + Σ a b^2 = our given expression (since includes both a^2b and ab^2). Indeed our expression is exactly Σ_{i≠j} a_i^2 a_j = Σ a^2 b + Σ a b^2 (the same). So we have:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799105325,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.79910644,"data":"       | Given expression = Σ a^2 b + Σ a b^2 = (a+b)(b+c)(c+a) - 2abc.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799107748,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799108844,"data":"       | Thus we have (a+b)(b+c)(c+a) = given + 2abc = 6,000,000 + 2abc.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.79911021,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799111283,"data":"       | But also we have identity: (a+b+c)^3 = a^3+b^3+c^3 + 3 (a+b)(b+c)(c+a).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799114295,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799115376,"data":"       | Given S=300, we have 27,000,000 = Σ a^3 + 3 (a+b)(b+c)(c+a).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799116612,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799117704,"data":"       | Thus Σ a^3 = 27,000,000 - 3 (a+b)(b+c)(c+a).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799118906,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.79912,"data":"       | Now earlier we derived Σ a^3 = 300 Σ a^2 - 6,000,000.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799121322,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799122403,"data":"       | Equate: 27,000,000 - 3P = 300 Σ a^2 - 6,000,000, where P = (a+b)(b+c)(c+a).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799123736,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799125018,"data":"       | Thus 300 Σ a^2 = 27,000,000 - 3P + 6,000,000 = 33,000,000 - 3P.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799126592,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799127708,"data":"       | Thus Σ a^2 = (33,000,000 - 3P)/300 = (33,000,000)/300 - (3P)/300 = 110,000 - P/100.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799128961,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799130186,"data":"       | Thus Σ a^2 = 110,000 - P/100.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799131385,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799132495,"data":"       | Since Σ a^2 is integer, P must be multiple of 100.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799133697,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799134846,"data":"       | Now also we have given expression G = Σ a^2 b + Σ a b^2 = P - 2abc = 6,000,000.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799136203,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799137278,"data":"       | Thus P = 6,000,000 + 2abc.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799138399,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799139642,"data":"       | Thus Σ a^2 = 110,000 - (6,000,000 + 2abc)/100 = 110,000 - 60,000 - (2abc)/100 = 50,000 - (2abc)/100 = 50,000 - (abc)/50.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799141,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799142189,"data":"       | Thus Σ a^2 = 50,000 - abc/50.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799143338,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799144511,"data":"       | Thus abc must be multiple of 50, and Σ a^2 = integer nonnegative.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799145772,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799146828,"data":"       | Now we also have sum = 300.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799147985,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799149056,"data":"       | We need to find nonnegative integer triples (a,b,c) such that:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799150299,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.79915137,"data":"       | 1) a+b+c = 300.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799152487,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799153548,"data":"       | 2) abc is multiple of 50 (i.e., abc = 50k for integer k≥0).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799154842,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799155909,"data":"       | 3) Σ a^2 = a^2+b^2+c^2 = 50,000 - abc/50.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799157079,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799158178,"data":"       | Since a,b,c nonnegative, left side nonnegative. So abc/50 ≤ 50,000 =\u003e abc ≤ 2,500,000.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799161338,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799162428,"data":"       | Also Σ a^2 must be nonnegative, automatically.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.79916365,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799164712,"data":"       | Now we can attempt to solve integer solutions.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799165925,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799167021,"data":"       | We also have expression for P = (a+b)(b+c)(c+a) = 6,000,000 + 2abc.\n"}
