,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799202419,"data":"       | Potentially we can solve by considering that a,b,c are nonnegative integers ≤300.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799205457,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799206602,"data":"       | We can attempt to brute-force search over all triples (a,b,c) with a+b+c=300. Number of such triples is C(300+3-1,3-1) = C(302,2) = 302*301/2 = 45,451. That's manageable to brute-force.\n"}
