,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799756105,"data":"       | Number of unordered multisets: Choose x in [0,200] but identify x and 200-x as same. So number of distinct unordered sets = floor(200/2)+1? Let's compute.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799757358,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799758407,"data":"       | If we consider unordered pair {x,200-x} with x ≤ 200-x (i.e., x ≤ 100). Then x ranges 0..100 inclusive. That's 101 possibilities. For each x, we have triple (100, x, 200-x). For x=100 gives triple (100,100,100). For other 100 values (x=0..99) we have distinct numbers, each giving 6 permutations.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799759943,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799760952,"data":"       | Thus total ordered triples = 1 (for x=100) + 100 * 6 = 1 + 600 = 601. Matches enumeration.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799762102,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799763124,"data":"       | Thus answer is 601.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799764161,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799765208,"data":"       | Now produce final answer.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799766264,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799767268,"data":"       | assistantfinal\\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.79976838,"data":"       | \\begin{aligned}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799769497,"data":"       | a+b+c \u0026=300 ,\\\\[2mm]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799770801,"data":"       | a^2b+a^2c+b^2a+b^2c+c^2a+c^2b \u0026=6\\,000\\,000 .\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799772238,"data":"       | \\end{aligned}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799773317,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799774363,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799787018,"data":"       | ---\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.79978898,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799790039,"data":"       | ### 1.  Express the second condition symmetrically  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799792773,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799793787,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799794976,"data":"       | \\begin{aligned}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.79979609,"data":"       | a^2b+a^2c+b^2a+b^2c+c^2a+c^2b\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799797218,"data":"       | \u0026=ab(a+b)+bc(b+c)+ca(c+a)\\\\\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799798448,"data":"       | \u0026=ab(300-c)+bc(300-a)+ca(300-b)\\\\\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799799675,"data":"       | \u0026=300(ab+bc+ca)-3abc .\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799800791,"data":"       | \\end{aligned}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799801869,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799802927,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799803938,"data":"       | Let  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799804965,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799805969,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799807017,"data":"       | S_1=a+b+c=300,\\qquad S_2=ab+bc+ca,\\qquad S_3=abc .\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799808242,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799809261,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799810277,"data":"       | Then  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799811341,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799812403,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799813478,"data":"       | 300S_2-3S_3=6\\,000\\,000\\Longrightarrow 100S_2-S_3=2\\,000\\,000 .\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799814806,"data":"       | \\tag{1}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799815869,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799816888,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799817878,"data":"       | ---\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799818899,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.79981992,"data":"       | ### 2.  A useful factorisation  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799821034,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799822041,"data":"       | Consider  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799823136,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799824117,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.79982517,"data":"       | (a-100)(b-100)(c-100).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799826235,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799827261,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799828286,"data":"       | Expanding and using \\(S_1=300\\),\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799829468,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799830456,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799831473,"data":"       | \\begin{aligned}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799832573,"data":"       | (a-100)(b-100)(c-100)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799834133,"data":"       | \u0026=abc-100(ab+bc+ca)+10\\,000(a+b+c)-1\\,000\\,000\\\\\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799835431,"data":"       | \u0026=S_3-100S_2+3\\,000\\,000-1\\,000\\,000\\\\\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799836705,"data":"       | \u0026=S_3-100S_2+2\\,000\\,000 .\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799837999,"data":"       | \\end{aligned}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799839076,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.79984009,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799843255,"data":"       | By (1) the last expression is zero, therefore  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799844516,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799845498,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799846519,"data":"       | \\boxed{(a-100)(b-100)(c-100)=0}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799847657,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799848816,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799849856,"data":"       | Hence at least one of the numbers equals \\(100\\).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799851073,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799852066,"data":"       | ---\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799853198,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799854211,"data":"       | ### 3.  Reduce to two variables  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799855301,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799856332,"data":"       | Assume \\(a=100\\) (the other cases are symmetric).  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799857699,"data":"       | Then \\(b+c=200\\) and\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799858869,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799859976,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799861017,"data":"       | \\begin{aligned}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799862089,"data":"       | \u0026100^2b+100^2c+b^2\\!100+b^2c+c^2\\!100+c^2b\\\\\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799863346,"data":"       | \u0026=300\\bigl(100b+100c+bc\\bigr)-3\\cdot100bc\\\\\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799864616,"data":"       | \u0026=300\\bigl(20\\,000+bc\\bigr)-300bc=6\\,000\\,000 .\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799865937,"data":"       | \\end{aligned}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799867006,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799868146,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799869205,"data":"       | Thus **any** non‑negative integers \\(b,c\\) with \\(b+c=200\\) satisfy the original equation.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799870612,"data":"       | Consequently every solution is a permutation of  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799871745,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799872748,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799873806,"data":"       | (100,\\;x,\\;200-x),\\qquad x=0,1,\\dots ,200 .\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799875068,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.79987609,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799877091,"data":"       | ---\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799878108,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799879125,"data":"       | ### 4.  Counting ordered triples  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799880203,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799881214,"data":"       | The unordered triples are obtained by taking \\(x\\le 200-x\\); i.e. \\(x=0,1,\\dots ,100\\).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799882641,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799883703,"data":"       | * For \\(x=100\\) we have \\((100,100,100)\\) – only **1** ordered triple.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799885113,"data":"       | * For each of the other \\(100\\) values (\\(x=0,\\dots ,99\\)) the three numbers are distinct, giving \\(3!=6\\) ordered permutations.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799886587,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.79988903,"data":"       | Hence  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799890151,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799891178,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799892198,"data":"       | N = 1 + 100\\cdot 6 = 601 .\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799893338,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799894361,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799895368,"data":"       | ---\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799896441,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.79989744,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799898488,"data":"       | \\boxed{601}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799900292,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.799901328,"data":"\n"}
