,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.801201773,"data":"       | = (a^2 b + a b^2) + (a^2 c + a c^2) + (b^2 c + b c^2) + 3 a b c.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.801202911,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.801203966,"data":"       | But Σ_{sym} a^2 b = a^2 b + a^2 c + b^2 a + b^2 c + c^2 a + c^2 b = (a^2 b + a b^2) + (a^2 c + a c^2) + (b^2 c + b c^2). That's exactly the sum of the first three groups above, which is (a+b+c)(ab+bc+ca) - 3abc.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.801205353,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.801206349,"data":"       | Thus E = S1*S2 - 3*S3.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.801207381,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.801208479,"data":"       | Given S1=300, E=6,000,000.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.801209564,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.801210822,"data":"       | Thus 300*S2 - 3*S3 = 6,000,000.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.801211879,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.801212905,"data":"       | Divide by 3: 100*S2 - S3 = 2,000,000.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.801213993,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.801214992,"data":"       | Thus S3 = 100*S2 - 2,000,000.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.80121604,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.801218314,"data":"       | We also have a,b,c nonnegative integers, sum fixed.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.801219449,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.801220504,"data":"       | Goal: count number of integer solutions (a,b,c) with these constraints.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.801221658,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.801222678,"data":"       | We need to consider possible values of S2 and S3 consistent with nonnegative integer a,b,c.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.801223861,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.801224919,"data":"       | We can think of enumerating possibilities? Since a,b,c up to 300 each.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.801226073,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.801227117,"data":"       | Brute force enumeration of all triples with sum 300 is about (300+2 choose 2)=~45k combos, which is fine. Could just brute force compute and count those satisfying equation. That would be easiest.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.801228453,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4109.801229468,"data":"       | But we must produce reasoning. However final answer is just number. Could compute via Python.\n"}
