,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.332713352,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.332714363,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.332715425,"data":"       | [10]=\\{1,2,\\dots ,10\\}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.332716557,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.3327176,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.332718648,"data":"       | and let a subset \\(S\\subseteq[10]\\) contain **exactly one** pair of consecutive integers.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.332719944,"data":"       | Denote that unique pair by \\(\\{k,k+1\\}\\) where \\(1\\le k\\le 9\\).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.332721297,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.332722351,"data":"       | --------------------------------------------------------------------\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.332723557,"data":"       | ### 1.  Structure of a valid subset\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.332724654,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.332725873,"data":"       | If \\(\\{k,k+1\\}\\subseteq S\\) is the only consecutive pair, then  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.33272715,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.332728184,"data":"       | * \\(k-1\\notin S\\) (otherwise \\(\\{k-1,k\\}\\) would be another pair),  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.332729497,"data":"       | * \\(k+2\\notin S\\) (otherwise \\(\\{k+1,k+2\\}\\) would be another pair).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.33273082,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.332731878,"data":"       | Hence the remaining elements of \\(S\\) must be chosen from the two\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.332733123,"data":"       | disjoint intervals  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.332734209,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.332735241,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.332737105,"data":"       | L_k=\\{1,2,\\dots ,k-2\\},\\qquad R_k=\\{k+3,k+4,\\dots ,10\\},\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.33273844,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.332739608,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.332740637,"data":"       | and **no two of those chosen elements may be consecutive** (otherwise a\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.332741825,"data":"       | new consecutive pair would appear).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.332742876,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.332744047,"data":"       | Thus for a fixed \\(k\\) the number of admissible subsets equals  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.33274525,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.332746257,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.332747312,"data":"       | \\#\\text{(no‑consecutive subsets of }L_k)\\times\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.332748785,"data":"       | \\#\\text{(no‑consecutive subsets of }R_k).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.332751647,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.332752751,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.332753922,"data":"       | --------------------------------------------------------------------\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.332755282,"data":"       | ### 2.  Subsets with no consecutive integers\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.332756509,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.332757552,"data":"       | For an interval of length \\(m\\) the number of subsets containing no\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.332758747,"data":"       | consecutive integers is the Fibonacci number \\(F_{m+2}\\) (with\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.332760001,"data":"       | \\(F_1=F_2=1\\)).  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.332761172,"data":"       | Indeed, let \\(a_m\\) be that number.  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.332762357,"data":"       | Either \\(m\\) is not chosen (giving \\(a_{m-1}\\) possibilities) or \\(m\\)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.332763668,"data":"       | is chosen (forcing \\(m-1\\) to be absent, giving \\(a_{m-2}\\) possibilities):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.332764928,"data":"       | \\(a_m=a_{m-1}+a_{m-2}\\) with \\(a_0=1,\\;a_1=2\\), so \\(a_m=F_{m+2}\\).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.332766344,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.332767348,"data":"       | --------------------------------------------------------------------\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.332768504,"data":"       | ### 3.  Counting for each position of the pair\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.332769644,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.33277067,"data":"       | For a given \\(k\\),\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.332771801,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.332772822,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.332773883,"data":"       | \\begin{aligned}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.332775018,"data":"       | |L_k| \u0026=\\max(0,k-2),\\\\\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.332784029,"data":"       | |R_k| \u0026=\\max\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4137.332785231,"data":"\n"}
