,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4191.578318661,"data":"       | Let integers be a,b with a,b \u003c 100, positive integers. Let d = gcd(a,b) = 3. So we can write a = 3x, b = 3y where x,y are positive integers, gcd(x,y)=1 (since factor 3 removed). Also a,b\u003c100 =\u003e x\u003c100/3 ≈33.33 =\u003e x ≤33, similarly y ≤33.\n"}
