,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4191.578333979,"data":"       | Now case 2: lcm = 12*b = 12*3y = 36y. So 3xy = 36y =\u003e divide by 3y (y\u003e0): x = 12. So x=12, y coprime to 12 (since gcd(x,y)=1). So y must be coprime to 12. Also y ≤33, and b=3y\u003c100 =\u003e y ≤33. So we need y ≤33, coprime to 12. Max y ≤33 coprime to 12 is also 31 (since 31 not divisible by 2 or 3). So y=31 gives b = 93, a=36. Sum also 129. So symmetric.\n"}
