,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4244.137618682,"data":"       | We need number of such paths that change direction exactly four times. That means number of times the direction (R or U) switches from one step to the next is exactly 4. So path consists of runs of consecutive same direction; number of runs = number of direction changes + 1 = 5 runs. Since we start with some direction (R or U) and then switch 4 times, total runs = 5.\n"}
