,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4244.137624441,"data":"       | We need to count sequences of runs: either start with R or start with U. Since runs alternate, there are 5 runs, odd number. So if start with R, the pattern is R-U-R-U-R (R runs at positions 1,3,5). That's 3 R runs and 2 U runs. If start with U, pattern U-R-U-R-U: 3 U runs and 2 R runs.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4244.137626125,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4244.137627228,"data":"       | Thus we need to count number of ways to split 8 R steps into 3 positive integer parts (since each run must have at least one step) for start with R case, and 8 U steps into 2 positive integer parts. Similarly for start with U case: split 8 U steps into 3 positive parts, 8 R steps into 2 positive parts.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4244.137628914,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4244.13763019,"data":"       | Also note that runs must be positive length (at least one step) because a direction change occurs only after at least one step of the previous direction.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4244.13763159,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4244.137632718,"data":"       | Thus number of ways for start with R: number of compositions of 8 into 3 positive parts times number of compositions of 8 into 2 positive parts.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4244.137634105,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4244.137635236,"data":"       | Number of compositions of n into k positive parts = C(n-1, k-1). So for 8 into 3: C(7,2)=21. For 8 into 2: C(7,1)=7.\n"}
