,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830528432,"data":"     [Reasoning] (2093 chars):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830529871,"data":"       | analysisWe need to solve for real numbers x\u003e1, y\u003e1 satisfying:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830531608,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830533062,"data":"       | log_x(y^x) = 10\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830534486,"data":"       | log_y(x^{4y}) = 10\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830536083,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830537505,"data":"       | We need xy.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830538918,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830540399,"data":"       | Let's translate:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830541806,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830543179,"data":"       | log base x of (y^x) = 10 =\u003e (y^x) = x^{10}. Wait: log_x(y^x) = 10 =\u003e y^x = x^{10}. Since log base a of b = c =\u003e b = a^c.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830544918,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830546585,"data":"       | Similarly, log_y(x^{4y}) = 10 =\u003e x^{4y} = y^{10}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830548132,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830549491,"data":"       | Thus we have system:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830550929,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830552299,"data":"       | 1) y^x = x^{10}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830564542,"data":"       | 2) x^{4y} = y^{10}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830565665,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830566666,"data":"       | We need x\u003e1, y\u003e1.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830567821,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830568859,"data":"       | We can try to solve system.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830569968,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830571026,"data":"       | Take logs: (Equation 1) x * ln y = 10 * ln x.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830572185,"data":"       | Equation 2: 4y * ln x = 10 * ln y.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830573262,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830574268,"data":"       | So we have:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830575289,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830576322,"data":"       | x ln y = 10 ln x  (A)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830577382,"data":"       | 4y ln x = 10 ln y  (B)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830578476,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830579498,"data":"       | We can treat unknowns x,y positive \u003e1.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830580671,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830581716,"data":"       | We can try to solve for ratio maybe.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830582828,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830583839,"data":"       | From (A): ln y = (10 ln x)/x.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830584891,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830585906,"data":"       | Plug into (B):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830586946,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830588119,"data":"       | 4y ln x = 10 * ((10 ln x)/x) =\u003e 4y ln x = (100 ln x)/x.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830589332,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830590336,"data":"       | Assuming ln x ≠ 0 (x\u003e1 =\u003e ln x\u003e0). Cancel ln x:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830592142,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830593272,"data":"       | 4y = 100 / x =\u003e y = 25 / x.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830594428,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830596456,"data":"       | Thus we have relation y = 25/x.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830597543,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830598645,"data":"       | Now substitute back into (A) or original.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830599793,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830600791,"data":"       | From (A): x ln y = 10 ln x.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830601862,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830602943,"data":"       | Plug y = 25/x.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830603949,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830604956,"data":"       | Compute ln y = ln(25/x) = ln 25 - ln x.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830606016,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830607118,"data":"       | Thus x (ln 25 - ln x) = 10 ln x.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830608191,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830609199,"data":"       | =\u003e x ln 25 - x ln x = 10 ln x.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830610328,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830611348,"data":"       | =\u003e x ln 25 = x ln x + 10 ln x = (x + 10) ln x.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830614462,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830615502,"data":"       | Thus (x + 10) ln x = x ln 25.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830616565,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830617611,"data":"       | =\u003e ln x = (x ln 25)/(x + 10).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830618739,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830619746,"data":"       | We can exponentiate: x = exp( (x ln 25)/(x+10) ).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830620923,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830621909,"data":"       | But we can solve numerically.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830623006,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830623996,"data":"       | Alternatively, we can manipulate algebraically.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830625113,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830626113,"data":"       | Let’s set t = ln x \u003e0. Then x = e^t.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830627402,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830628478,"data":"       | Equation (A) becomes:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830629558,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.83063056,"data":"       | x ln y = 10 ln x =\u003e e^t * ln y = 10 t.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830631719,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830632898,"data":"       | But we have relation y = 25/x = 25 e^{-t}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830634028,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830635132,"data":"       | Thus ln y = ln 25 - t.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830636296,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830637305,"data":"       | Plug: e^t * (ln 25 - t) = 10 t.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830638356,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830639482,"data":"       | =\u003e e^t (ln 25 - t) = 10 t.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830640565,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830641576,"data":"       | Now we need to solve for t \u003e0.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.83064268,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830643789,"data":"       | Define f(t) = e^t (ln 25 - t) - 10 t = 0.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830644909,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830645892,"data":"       | We can solve numerically.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.83064695,"data":"       | \n"}
