,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830885782,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830886829,"data":"       | First equation: log base x of (y^x) = 10 =\u003e (y^x) = x^{10}. Since log_x(A)=10 =\u003e A = x^{10}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830888106,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830889115,"data":"       | Thus y^x = x^{10}. (1)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830890172,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.830891382,"data":"       | Second: log base y of (x^{4y}) = 10 =\u003e x^{4y} = y^{10}. (2)\n"}
