,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831170592,"data":"       | analysisWe need to solve for real numbers x\u003e1, y\u003e1 such that:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831171792,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831172799,"data":"       | log_x(y^x) = 10\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831173942,"data":"       | log_y(x^{4y}) = 10\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831175018,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831176755,"data":"       | We need xy.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831177985,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831178999,"data":"       | Let’s translate: log base x of y^x = 10 =\u003e y^x = x^{10}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831180313,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831181339,"data":"       | Second: log base y of x^{4y} = 10 =\u003e x^{4y} = y^{10}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831182629,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831183675,"data":"       | Thus we have system:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831184756,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831185871,"data":"       | (1) y^x = x^{10}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831187099,"data":"       | (2) x^{4y} = y^{10}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831189785,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831190796,"data":"       | Both x,y\u003e1.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831191873,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831192862,"data":"       | We need xy.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831193902,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831194919,"data":"       | Let’s take logs: natural logs.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831196028,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831197029,"data":"       | Equation (1): x ln y = 10 ln x.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831198091,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831199102,"data":"       | Equation (2): 4y ln x = 10 ln y.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831200158,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831201205,"data":"       | Let’s denote a = ln x, b = ln y. Since x\u003e1 =\u003e a\u003e0, y\u003e1 =\u003e b\u003e0.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831202752,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831203772,"data":"       | Then equations become:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831204822,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831206019,"data":"       | (1) x ln y = e^{a} * b = 10 a. Wait careful: x = e^{a}, y = e^{b}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831207149,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831208889,"data":"       | Equation (1): y^x = x^{10} =\u003e (e^{b})^{e^{a}} = (e^{a})^{10} =\u003e e^{b e^{a}} = e^{10 a} =\u003e b e^{a} = 10 a.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831210158,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831211375,"data":"       | Equation (2): x^{4y} = y^{10} =\u003e (e^{a})^{4 e^{b}} = (e^{b})^{10} =\u003e e^{a * 4 e^{b}} = e^{10 b} =\u003e 4 a e^{b} = 10 b.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831212696,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831213696,"data":"       | Thus we have system:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831214741,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831215881,"data":"       | (1') b e^{a} = 10 a\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831216929,"data":"       | (2') 4 a e^{b} = 10 b\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831217983,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831219019,"data":"       | We need xy = e^{a+b}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831220166,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831221196,"data":"       | We can attempt to solve for a,b.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831222242,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831223246,"data":"       | Let’s rewrite:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831224472,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831225485,"data":"       | b e^{a} = 10 a   =\u003e b = 10 a e^{-a}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831226593,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831227619,"data":"       | Similarly, 4 a e^{b} = 10 b =\u003e divide both sides by a (a\u003e0): 4 e^{b} = 10 b / a =\u003e e^{b} = (10 b)/(4 a) = (5 b)/(2 a).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831228902,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831229935,"data":"       | Thus e^{b} = (5 b)/(2 a). (Equation A)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831231019,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831232038,"data":"       | But also from first expression we have b expressed in terms of a: b = 10 a e^{-a}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831238429,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831239455,"data":"       | Plug into equation A:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831240473,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831241506,"data":"       | e^{b} = (5 b)/(2 a) = (5 * (10 a e^{-a}))/(2 a) = (50 a e^{-a})/(2 a) = 25 e^{-a}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831242676,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831243716,"data":"       | Thus e^{b} = 25 e^{-a}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831244736,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831245742,"data":"       | Take natural logs: b = ln 25 - a.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831246795,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831247828,"data":"       | But we also have b = 10 a e^{-a}. So:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831248886,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831249982,"data":"       | 10 a e^{-a} = ln 25 - a.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831251188,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831252292,"data":"       | Thus we need to solve for a\u003e0.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831253411,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831254439,"data":"       | Let’s set up equation:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831255508,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831256521,"data":"       | 10 a e^{-a} + a = ln 25.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831257576,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831258598,"data":"       | =\u003e a (10 e^{-a} + 1) = ln 25.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831259672,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831260733,"data":"       | Let’s denote L = ln 25 = ln(5^2) = 2 ln 5 ≈ 2*1.609437912 = 3.218875824.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831261922,"data":"       | \n"}
