,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831829516,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831830585,"data":"       | Equation A: (e^a) * b = 10 a. (since x ln y = e^a * b = 10 a)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831831729,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831832759,"data":"       | Equation B: 4 (e^b) * a = 10 b. (since 4 y ln x = 4 e^b * a = 10 b)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831833886,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831834878,"data":"       | Thus:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831835936,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831836938,"data":"       | (1) b e^a = 10 a\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831838019,"data":"       | (2) 4 a e^b = 10 b\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831839065,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831840063,"data":"       | We can rearrange.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831841111,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831842136,"data":"       | From (1): b = (10 a) / e^a.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831843225,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831844228,"data":"       | Plug into (2):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831845269,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831846316,"data":"       | 4 a e^b = 10 * ((10 a) / e^a) =\u003e 4 a e^b = (100 a) / e^a\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831847466,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831848505,"data":"       | Assuming a\u003e0 (since x\u003e1). Cancel a (non-zero). So:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831849679,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831850688,"data":"       | 4 e^b = 100 / e^a\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831851735,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831852738,"data":"       | =\u003e e^b = (100 / e^a) / 4 = 25 / e^a\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831853861,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831854909,"data":"       | Thus e^b = 25 e^{-a}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831855951,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831856985,"data":"       | But e^b = y, e^{-a} = 1/x.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831858035,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831859058,"data":"       | So y = 25 / x.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831860095,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831861342,"data":"       | Now we have relation y = 25/x.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831862519,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831863652,"data":"       | Plug into original equation (maybe easier). Let's verify.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831864769,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831865759,"data":"       | Given y = 25/x.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831866788,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831867798,"data":"       | We need x\u003e1, y\u003e1 =\u003e 25/x \u003e1 =\u003e x\u003c25.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831869073,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831870081,"data":"       | Also x\u003e1.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831871158,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831872213,"data":"       | Now plug into equation (1) y^x = x^{10}. Write (25/x)^x = x^{10}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831873366,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831876028,"data":"       | Take logs: x ln (25/x) = 10 ln x.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831877135,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831878143,"data":"       | Compute: x (ln 25 - ln x) = 10 ln x\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831879205,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831880211,"data":"       | =\u003e x ln 25 - x ln x = 10 ln x\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831881325,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831882355,"data":"       | =\u003e x ln 25 = (x + 10) ln x\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831883432,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831884431,"data":"       | =\u003e ln 25 = ((x + 10)/x) ln x = (1 + 10/x) ln x.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831885562,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831886615,"data":"       | Thus we need to solve for x\u003e1 (and \u003c25) satisfying:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831888038,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831889039,"data":"       | ln 25 = (1 + 10/x) ln x.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831890242,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831891265,"data":"       | Let’s set up equation.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831892358,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831893375,"data":"       | Let’s solve numerically.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831894551,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831895572,"data":"       | But perhaps there is a rational solution? Let's attempt to guess.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831896695,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831897729,"data":"       | Let’s exponentiate both sides: 25 = x^{1 + 10/x} = x * x^{10/x}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831899036,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831900049,"data":"       | Thus 25 = x * x^{10/x}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831901066,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831902055,"data":"       | So x^{10/x} = 25 / x.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831903222,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831904242,"data":"       | Let’s define t = x. This equation may have integer solution maybe x=5? Let's test.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831905412,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831906438,"data":"       | If x=5, then RHS = 25/5 =5. LHS: x^{10/x}=5^{10/5}=5^{2}=25. Wait LHS = 25, RHS=5. Not equal.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831907601,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831908649,"data":"       | If x=10, RHS=25/10=2.5, LHS=10^{10/10}=10^{1}=10. Not equal.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831909776,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831910766,"data":"       | If x=25? Not allowed (since y\u003e1). x=25 =\u003e y=1, not allowed.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831911948,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831912956,"data":"       | If x=4? RHS=25/4=6.25, LHS=4^{10/4}=4^{2.5}=4^{2} * 4^{0.5}=16 *2=32. Not equal.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831914094,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831915121,"data":"       | If x=2? RHS=12.5, LHS=2^{5}=32. Not equal.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831916209,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831917262,"data":"       | If x=3? RHS=25/3≈8.333, LHS=3^{10/3}=3^{3.333...}=3^{3} * 3^{0.333}=27 * 3^{1/3}≈27*1.442=38.9.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831920362,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831921406,"data":"       | Seems LHS \u003e RHS for small x.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831922481,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831923545,"data":"       | Maybe x\u003e10? Let's test x=20: RHS=25/20=1.25, LHS=20^{10/20}=20^{0.5}=sqrt(20)≈4.472. LHS\u003eRHS.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831924855,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831925876,"data":"       | At x=24: RHS≈25/24≈1.0417, LHS=24^{10/24}=24^{0.4167}=exp(0.4167 ln 24)=exp(0.4167*3.178)=exp(1.324)=3.76 \u003e1.04.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831927192,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831928439,"data":"       | Seems LHS \u003e RHS for all x? Let's test near 25? x=24.9: RHS≈1.004, LHS=24.9^{10/24.9}=exp((10/24.9) ln 24.9)=exp(0.4016*3.214)=exp(1.291)=3.64 \u003e1. So LHS still \u003e RHS.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831929899,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831930958,"data":"       | But at x close to 25, RHS ~1, LHS \u003e1. So LHS\u003eRHS for all x? Let's test x close to 1? x=1.1: RHS=25/1.1≈22.727, LHS=1.1^{10/1.1}=1.1^{9.0909}=exp(9.0909*ln1.1)=exp(9.0909*0.09531)=exp(0.866)=2.378. So LHS\u003cRHS now.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831932482,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831933545,"data":"       | Thus there is crossing somewhere between 1.1 and maybe 5? At x=2, LHS=32, RHS=12.5 (LHS\u003eRHS). At x=1.5: RHS=25/1.5≈16.667, LHS=1.5^{10/1.5}=1.5^{6.6667}=exp(6.6667*ln1.5)=exp(6.6667*0.4055)=exp(2.703)=14.92. LHS\u003cRHS? 14.92\u003c16.667, yes LHS\u003cRHS.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831935142,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.831936165,"data":"       | At x=1.6: RHS=25/1.6=15.625, LHS=1.6^{10/1.6}=1.6^{6.25}=exp(6.25*ln1.6)=exp(6.25*0.4700)=exp(2.9375)=18.85 \u003e15.625. So crossing between 1.5 and 1.6.\n"}
