,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832345951,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832346969,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832348085,"data":"       | e^{\\,b}= \\frac{25}{e^{a}} .\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832349181,"data":"       | \\tag{4}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832350235,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832351235,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832352246,"data":"       | Multiplying (4) by \\(e^{a}\\) gives  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832353374,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832354361,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832355375,"data":"       | e^{a+b}=25 .\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832356448,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832357432,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832358454,"data":"       | But \\(e^{a}=x\\) and \\(e^{b}=y\\); therefore  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832359685,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832360672,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832361671,"data":"       | xy = e^{a+b}=25 .\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832362722,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832363719,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832364762,"data":"       | ---\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832365776,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832366785,"data":"       | ### 4.  Existence of a solution  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832367832,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832368849,"data":"       | Equation (3) together with \\(b=\\ln 25-a\\) (from \\(e^{a+b}=25\\)) yields  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832370178,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832371176,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832372201,"data":"       | \\ln 25-a=\\frac{10a}{e^{a}} .\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832373354,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832374366,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832375456,"data":"       | The left‑hand side decreases from \\(\\ln 25\\) to \\(-\\infty\\) as \\(a\\) increases, while the right‑hand side is positive and tends to \\(0\\). Hence a unique positive \\(a\\) (and consequently \\(b\u003e0\\)) satisfies the equation, giving \\(x\u003e1,\\;y\u003e1\\).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832377409,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832378446,"data":"       | Thus a pair \\((x,y)\\) with the required properties exists, and the product is uniquely determined.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832381366,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832382386,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832383402,"data":"       | \\boxed{25}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832384481,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832385508,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832386502,"data":"     - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832387782,"data":"     ATTEMPT 7  |  answer=25  entropy=0.383  code_calls=5  errors=0  tokens=1947  time=18.4s \u003c\u003c CORRECT\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832389039,"data":"     - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832390169,"data":"     Libraries: import mpmath as mp | import mpmath as mp, math, sys, sympy as sp\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832391311,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832392321,"data":"     [Turn 1]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832393504,"data":"     [Reasoning] (2477 chars):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832394546,"data":"       | analysisWe need to solve for real numbers x\u003e1, y\u003e1 such that:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832395731,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832396779,"data":"       | log_x ( y^x ) = 10\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832397799,"data":"       | log_y ( x^{4y} ) = 10\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832398862,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832399866,"data":"       | Interpret logs: log base a of b = ln(b)/ln(a). So we have:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832400985,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832402021,"data":"       | ln(y^x) / ln x = 10 =\u003e (x ln y) / ln x = 10 =\u003e x ln y = 10 ln x ... (1)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832403234,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832404479,"data":"       | Second: ln(x^{4y}) / ln y = 10 =\u003e (4y ln x) / ln y = 10 =\u003e 4y ln x = 10 ln y =\u003e 4y ln x = 10 ln y ... (2)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832405759,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832406759,"data":"       | We have two equations:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832407806,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832408818,"data":"       | x ln y = 10 ln x\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832409842,"data":"       | 4y ln x = 10 ln y\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832410915,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832411905,"data":"       | We need xy.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832412942,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832413952,"data":"       | We can treat unknowns positive \u003e1.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832415062,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832416071,"data":"       | Let’s denote a = ln x, b = ln y. Then x = e^a, y = e^b, a\u003e0, b\u003e0.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832417301,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832418306,"data":"       | Equations become:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832419345,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832420356,"data":"       | (e^a) * b = 10 * a   (since x ln y = e^a * b)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832421472,"data":"       | 4 (e^b) * a = 10 * b   (since 4 y ln x = 4 e^b * a = 10 b)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832424048,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832425056,"data":"       | Thus:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832426071,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832427085,"data":"       | b e^a = 10 a   (1')\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832428134,"data":"       | 4 a e^b = 10 b   (2')\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832429211,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832430246,"data":"       | We need xy = e^{a+b} = e^{a+b}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832431322,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832432338,"data":"       | We have two equations in a,b.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832433384,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832434392,"data":"       | Let's solve.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832435416,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832436445,"data":"       | From (1'): b e^a = 10 a =\u003e b = 10 a e^{-a}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832437575,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832438592,"data":"       | Plug into (2'): 4 a e^b = 10 b =\u003e 4 a e^{b} = 10 b.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832439745,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832440754,"data":"       | Substitute b expression:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832441801,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832442855,"data":"       | b = 10 a e^{-a}. Then RHS: 10 b = 10 * (10 a e^{-a}) = 100 a e^{-a}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832443982,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832445012,"data":"       | LHS: 4 a e^{b} = 4 a e^{10 a e^{-a}}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832446109,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832447109,"data":"       | Thus equation:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832448138,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832449131,"data":"       | 4 a e^{10 a e^{-a}} = 100 a e^{-a}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832450218,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832451248,"data":"       | Assuming a\u003e0, we can divide both sides by a (nonzero). So:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832452392,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832453402,"data":"       | 4 e^{10 a e^{-a}} = 100 e^{-a}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832454492,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832455521,"data":"       | Divide both sides by 4:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832456554,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832457569,"data":"       | e^{10 a e^{-a}} = 25 e^{-a}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832458649,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832459754,"data":"       | Take natural log:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832460785,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832461785,"data":"       | 10 a e^{-a} = ln 25 - a.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832462946,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832464016,"data":"       | Thus:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832465039,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832466031,"data":"       | 10 a e^{-a} + a = ln 25.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832467096,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832468196,"data":"       | =\u003e a (10 e^{-a} + 1) = ln 25.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832470646,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832471676,"data":"       | Thus a = ln 25 / (1 + 10 e^{-a}).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832472759,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832473842,"data":"       | But this is implicit.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832474868,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832475871,"data":"       | We can solve numerically for a\u003e0.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832476975,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832478012,"data":"       | Alternatively maybe there is a simple solution with integer/ rational a? Let's attempt.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832479161,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832480201,"data":"       | Let’s set t = e^{-a}. Then a = -ln t, with t in (0,1). Then e^{-a} = t.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832481401,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832482434,"data":"       | Equation: 10 a e^{-a} = ln 25 - a.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832483495,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832484626,"data":"       | =\u003e 10 (-ln t) t = ln 25 + ln t? Wait compute: a = -ln t.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832485791,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832486789,"data":"       | Plug: 10 a e^{-a} = 10 (-ln t) * t = -10 t ln t.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832487891,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832488918,"data":"       | Right side: ln 25 - a = ln 25 - (-ln t) = ln 25 + ln t = ln(25 t).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832490062,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832491046,"data":"       | Thus equation: -10 t ln t = ln(25 t).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832492124,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832493129,"data":"       | Multiply both sides by -1: 10 t ln t = -ln(25 t) = ln( (25 t)^{-1}) = ln(1/(25 t)).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832494291,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832495306,"data":"       | Thus we have:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832496322,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832497321,"data":"       | 10 t ln t = ln(1/(25 t)).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832498416,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832499436,"data":"       | Exponentiate both sides? Not straightforward because left side is product.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832500594,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832501581,"data":"       | Let’s attempt to solve numerically.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832502676,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832503706,"data":"       | But maybe there is a nice solution where t is rational power of something.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832504848,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832505846,"data":"       | Let’s try to solve using python.assistantanalysis to=python codeimport mpmath as mp\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4263.832507028,"data":"       | \n"}
