,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.707378256,"data":"       | But we should also confirm that the functional equation indeed has a unique solution elsewhere. Let's solve for f(x) generally when D != 0:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.70737962,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.707380699,"data":"       | f(x) = (A(x) * (1 - x)^2 - B(x)) / D? Let's compute using matrix inversion.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.707381979,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.707384822,"data":"       | Given system: [a b; c d] * [f(x); f(1 - x)] = [A; B] where a = x^2, b = 1, c = 1, d = (1 - x)^2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.707386126,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.70738723,"data":"       | Inverse matrix: 1/D * [d, -b; -c, a] . So f(x) = (d*A - b*B)/D = ((1 - x)^2 * A - B) / D.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.707388509,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.70738962,"data":"       | We can compute expression and see if defined for all x except α,β. Let's compute symbolic to confirm.assistantanalysis to=python codex=sp.symbols('x')\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.707391062,"data":"       | A = -x**4 + 2*x\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.707392206,"data":"       | B = -(1-x)**4 + 2*(1-x)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.707393346,"data":"       | D = x**2 * (1-x)**2 - 1\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.70739447,"data":"       | f_expr = sp.simplify(((1-x)**2 * A - B) / D)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.707395707,"data":"       | sp.simplify(f_expr)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.707396844,"data":"       | \n"}
