,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.707413577,"data":"       | analysisInteresting! f(x) = 1 - x^2 for all x where D != 0. Let's verify: plug into original equation: x^2 (1 - x^2) + (1 - (1 - x)^2) =? compute.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.707414964,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.70741653,"data":"       | Compute: x^2 (1 - x^2) = x^2 - x^4. f(1 - x) = 1 - (1 - x)^2 = 1 - (1 - 2x + x^2) = 2x - x^2. Sum: (x^2 - x^4) + (2x - x^2) = -x^4 + 2x, matches RHS. So indeed f(x) = 1 - x^2 satisfies equation for all x. But at α and β, D=0, the expression for f(x) derived via solving linear system would have denominator zero, but the function 1 - x^2 is still defined there. However the functional equation does not uniquely determine f at those points; there may be other functions that also satisfy the equation, differing only at those points. Indeed because the linear equations become dependent, we can assign arbitrary values to f(α) and f(β) that still satisfy the functional equation? Let's verify.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.707419,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.707420162,"data":"       | At x = α, equation (1) becomes α^2 f(α) + f(1 - α) = -α^4 + 2α. But 1 - α = β. So we have α^2 f(α) + f(β) = RHS. Similarly at x = β, we have β^2 f(β) + f(α) = -β^4 + 2β. These two equations are dependent (since coefficient matrix singular). So there is a one-parameter family of solutions for (f(α), f(β)). Indeed we can solve for relationship.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.70742444,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.70742558,"data":"       | Thus function is uniquely determined elsewhere as 1 - x^2, but at α,β there is a degree of freedom. So answer α^2 + β^2 = 3.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.707426998,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.7074281,"data":"       | Thus final answer: 3.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.707429207,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.70743033,"data":"       | Now produce final output.assistantfinalThe functional equation  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.707431544,"data":"       | \n"}
