,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.707937622,"data":"       | Now we have two linear equations in unknowns f(x) and f(1 - x). Solve for f(x). However, the coefficient matrix may be singular for some x values, causing non-uniqueness (i.e., infinite solutions). Those x values correspond to α and β.\n"}
