,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708079222,"data":"       | analysisIt returns zero! So our earlier manual computation gave wrong expression for RHS2. Let's compute again correctly.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708080548,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.70808193,"data":"       | We used relation 1 - x = -1/x, but maybe sign? Let's verify: x(1 - x) = -1 =\u003e 1 - x = -1/x. That's correct.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708083282,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708084406,"data":"       | Now compute RHS2 = -(1 - x)^4 + 2(1 - x). Since (1 - x) = -1/x, (1 - x)^4 = (1/x)^4 = 1/x^4. So -(1 - x)^4 = -1/x^4.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708085702,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708086758,"data":"       | And 2(1 - x) = 2(-1/x) = -2/x.\n"}
