,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708090414,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708091484,"data":"       | Now compute RHS1 / x^2 = (-x^4 + 2x)/x^2 = -x^2 + 2/x.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708092643,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708093709,"data":"       | Set RHS2 = RHS1/x^2 =\u003e -1/x^4 - 2/x = -x^2 + 2/x.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708094988,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708096064,"data":"       | Multiply both sides by x^4: -1 - 2 x^3 = -x^6 + 2 x^3.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708097277,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708098368,"data":"       | =\u003e bring all: -1 - 2 x^3 + x^6 - 2 x^3 = 0 =\u003e x^6 - 4 x^3 - 1 = 0.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708099689,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708100787,"data":"       | But we also have condition x(1 - x) = -1 =\u003e x - x^2 = -1 =\u003e x^2 - x - 1 = 0 =\u003e x satisfies quadratic.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708102151,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708103246,"data":"       | Now does quadratic solution also satisfy the sextic? Let's test: plug x satisfying x^2 - x - 1 = 0 into x^6 - 4 x^3 - 1. Use sympy.assistantanalysis to=python codex=sp.symbols('x')\n"}
