,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708280544,"data":"       | But we should also ensure that there is indeed a function f that satisfies the equation for all real x, despite indeterminacy at α, β. The functional equation imposes constraints for all x, but at x = α, β we have only one independent equation linking f(α) and f(β). So we can choose any value for f(α) (or f(β)), then compute the other using the equation. So there are infinitely many functions satisfying the equation, but f is uniquely determined except at those points.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708285216,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708286332,"data":"       | Thus answer: 3.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.70828745,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708288596,"data":"       | Now produce final answer.assistantfinalThe functional equation  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708289816,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708290864,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708292004,"data":"       | x^{2}f(x)+f(1-x)=-x^{4}+2x \\qquad(\\forall x\\in\\mathbb R)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708293321,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708294469,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708295553,"data":"       | relates the two values \\(f(x)\\) and \\(f(1-x)\\).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708296845,"data":"       | Write the equation for \\(x\\) and for \\(1-x\\):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708298125,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708299189,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708300297,"data":"       | \\begin{cases}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708301445,"data":"       | x^{2}f(x)+f(1-x)= -x^{4}+2x,\\\\[2mm]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708302673,"data":"       | f(x)+(1-x)^{2}f(1-x)=-(1-x)^{4}+2(1-x).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708303865,"data":"       | \\end{cases}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708304984,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708306061,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708307147,"data":"       | Let  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708308244,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708309304,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708310427,"data":"       | A=f(x),\\qquad B=f(1-x).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.7083116,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708312746,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.70831392,"data":"       | Then  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708315194,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708316265,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708317357,"data":"       | \\begin{pmatrix}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708318514,"data":"       | x^{2} \u0026 1\\\\[1mm]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708319726,"data":"       | 1 \u0026 (1-x)^{2}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708320907,"data":"       | \\end{pmatrix}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708322139,"data":"       | \\begin{pmatrix}A\\\\B\\end{pmatrix}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708323396,"data":"       | =\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708324502,"data":"       | \\begin{pmatrix}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708325654,"data":"       | -x^{4}+2x\\\\[1mm]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708326786,"data":"       | -(1-x)^{4}+2(1-x)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.7083279,"data":"       | \\end{pmatrix}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708329048,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708330125,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708332847,"data":"       | The determinant of the coefficient matrix is  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708334061,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708335145,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708336251,"data":"       | \\Delta = x^{2}(1-x)^{2}-1 =\\bigl[x(1-x)\\bigr]^{2}-1 .\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.70833751,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708338602,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.70833974,"data":"       | If \\(\\Delta\\neq0\\) the system has a unique solution, giving a unique value for\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708341076,"data":"       | \\(f(x)\\) (and also for \\(f(1-x)\\)).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.70834239,"data":"       | Thus indeterminacy occurs exactly when  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708343531,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708344633,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708345768,"data":"       | \\Delta =0\\Longleftrightarrow x^{2}(1-x)^{2}=1\\Longleftrightarrow x(1-x)=\\pm1 .\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708347148,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708348213,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708349336,"data":"       | The case \\(x(1-x)=1\\) gives \\(x^{2}-x+1=0\\), which has no real roots.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708350684,"data":"       | The case \\(x(1-x)=-1\\) gives  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708351935,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708352989,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708354102,"data":"       | x^{2}-x-1=0,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708355223,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708356304,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708357402,"data":"       | whose real solutions are  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708358566,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708359649,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708360792,"data":"       | \\alpha=\\frac{1+\\sqrt5}{2},\\qquad \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708362043,"data":"       | \\beta =\\frac{1-\\sqrt5}{2}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708363243,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708364344,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708365564,"data":"       | For these two numbers the two equations above are linearly dependent\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708366838,"data":"       | (the rows of the matrix are scalar multiples), so only one relation\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708368206,"data":"       | between \\(f(\\alpha)\\) and \\(f(\\beta)\\) is obtained; each of the two values\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708369574,"data":"       | can be chosen arbitrarily, and the other is then fixed.  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708371003,"data":"       | Hence \\(f\\) is uniquely determined for all real \\(x\\) except at\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708372361,"data":"       | \\(x=\\alpha\\) and \\(x=\\beta\\).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708373769,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708374852,"data":"       | Finally,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.70837609,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708377159,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708378335,"data":"       | \\alpha^{2}+\\beta^{2}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.70838117,"data":"       | =(\\alpha+\\beta)^{2}-2\\alpha\\beta\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708382598,"data":"       | =1^{2}-2(-1)=1+2=3 .\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.70838373,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708384946,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708386007,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708387241,"data":"       | \\boxed{3}\n"}
