,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708508072,"data":"       | Let's craft final answer accordingly.assistantfinalThe functional equation  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708509294,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708510356,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708511523,"data":"       | x^{2}f(x)+f(1-x)=-x^{4}+2x\\qquad(\\forall x\\in\\mathbb R)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708512831,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708513932,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708515044,"data":"       | relates the two values \\(f(x)\\) and \\(f(1-x)\\).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708516426,"data":"       | Write the same equation for the argument \\(1-x\\):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.70851766,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.70851872,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708519838,"data":"       | (1-x)^{2}f(1-x)+f(x)=-(1-x)^{4}+2(1-x).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708520989,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708522088,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708523169,"data":"       | For each fixed \\(x\\) we have a linear system in the unknowns\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.70852448,"data":"       | \\(f(x)\\) and \\(f(1-x)\\):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708525655,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708526703,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708527853,"data":"       | \\begin{cases}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708529692,"data":"       | x^{2}f(x)+f(1-x)= -x^{4}+2x,\\\\[2mm]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708530928,"data":"       | f(x)+(1-x)^{2}f(1-x)= -(1-x)^{4}+2(1-x).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708532192,"data":"       | \\end{cases}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708533326,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708534544,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708535626,"data":"       | The coefficient matrix is  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708536841,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708537914,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708539109,"data":"       | A=\\begin{pmatrix}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708540378,"data":"       | x^{2} \u0026 1\\\\\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708541709,"data":"       | 1 \u0026 (1-x)^{2}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708542859,"data":"       | \\end{pmatrix},\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708544262,"data":"       | \\qquad\\det A = x^{2}(1-x)^{2}-1\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708547736,"data":"       |           =\\bigl[x(1-x)\\bigr]^{2}-1 .\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708549074,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708550168,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708551389,"data":"       | If \\(\\det A\\neq 0\\) the system has a unique solution, giving a unique\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708552677,"data":"       | value of \\(f(x)\\) (and also of \\(f(1-x)\\)).  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708554118,"data":"       | Thus the only points where \\(f\\) may fail to be uniquely determined are the real\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708555471,"data":"       | solutions of  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.70855662,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708557691,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708558822,"data":"       | \\bigl[x(1-x)\\bigr]^{2}=1.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708559996,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708561095,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708562182,"data":"       | Since \\((x(1-x))^{2}=1\\) gives \\(x(1-x)=\\pm1\\), we solve\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708563514,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708564556,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708565708,"data":"       | \\begin{aligned}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708566856,"data":"       | x(1-x)=1 \u0026\\Longrightarrow x^{2}-x+1=0\\quad(\\text{no real root}),\\\\\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708568258,"data":"       | x(1-x)=-1 \u0026\\Longrightarrow x^{2}-x-1=0.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708569485,"data":"       | \\end{aligned}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708570569,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708571666,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708572746,"data":"       | The quadratic \\(x^{2}-x-1=0\\) has the real roots  \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708574008,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708575104,"data":"       | \\[\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708576192,"data":"       | \\alpha=\\frac{1+\\sqrt5}{2},\\qquad \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708577386,"data":"       | \\beta =\\frac{1-\\sqrt5}{2},\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708578572,"data":"       | \\]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708579644,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708580758,"data":"       | and indeed \\(\\alpha+\\beta=1\\), so \\(1-\\alpha=\\beta\\) and \\(1-\\beta=\\alpha\\).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708582302,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708583384,"data":"       | At \\(x=\\alpha\\) (and similarly at \\(x=\\beta\\)) the two equations above are\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708584789,"data":"       | linearly dependent, giving only one relation between \\(f(\\alpha)\\) and\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708586102,"data":"       | \\(f(\\beta)\\). Hence \\(f(\\alpha)\\) and \\(f(\\beta)\\) are not uniquely determined,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708587523,"data":"       | while \\(f(x)\\) is uniquely determined for every other real \\(x\\).\n"}
