,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4291.708892661,"data":"       | When D=0, the two equations are linearly dependent; i.e., one is a multiple of the other. That means we have only one independent equation for two unknowns, leading to infinite solutions unless the RHS also satisfy same relation (i.e., they are consistent). But the functional equation ensures that both equations hold; they might be consistent (i.e., the RHS satisfy same linear dependence). In that case, we cannot uniquely determine f(x) and f(1 - x); there will be infinitely many solutions (one degree of freedom). So α and β correspond to the two x values where D=0.\n"}
