,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.192629322,"data":"       | Thus three possible D's:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.192630366,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.192631384,"data":"       | 1) D1 = B + C - A (if A is common vertex)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.192632511,"data":"       | 2) D2 = A + C - B (if B is common vertex)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.19263367,"data":"       | 3) D3 = A + B - C (if C is common vertex)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.192635025,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.192636062,"data":"       | Now we need perimeters of the parallelogram for each case. However note that the perimeter depends on side lengths: opposite sides equal. For each configuration, the side lengths are lengths of vectors between adjacent vertices.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.192637486,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.192638494,"data":"       | Let's compute lengths for each case.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.192639587,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.192640596,"data":"       | But we also need \"greatest possible perimeter\" and \"least possible perimeter\" among all possible parallelograms formed by these three vertices (i.e., among the three possible D). Then compute positive difference between greatest and least perimeters.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.192642204,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.192643237,"data":"       | Let's compute using Python.assistantanalysis to=python codeimport sympy as sp\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.192644394,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.192645387,"data":"       | A = sp.Point(-1,0)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.192646429,"data":"       | B = sp.Point(2,4)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.192647489,"data":"       | C = sp.Point(2,-4)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.192648542,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.192651107,"data":"       | def perimeter_given_common(common):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.192652242,"data":"       |     # common is point name: 'A','B','C'\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.192653386,"data":"       |     if common == 'A':\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.192654421,"data":"       |         D = B + C - A\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.192655569,"data":"       |         # vertices order: A, B, D, C? Need adjacency: A adjacent to B and C.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.192656741,"data":"       |         # So sides: AB, AC, opposite sides: CD, BD? Wait we need shape.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.192657942,"data":"       |         # Let's order: A (common) adjacent to B and C. So quadrilateral: A-B-? -C? Actually typical order: A (common), then B, then D (opposite A), then C, back to A.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.192659235,"data":"       |         # Let's verify: D = B + C - A. Then vector AB = B-A, vector AC = C-A.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.192660394,"data":"       |         # Opposite sides: B-D should be equal to AC, and C-D equal to AB.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.192661543,"data":"       |         # So order A-B-D-C forms parallelogram.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.192662699,"data":"       |         order = [A, B, D, C]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.192663801,"data":"       |     elif common == 'B':\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.192664901,"data":"       |         D = A + C - B\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.192666006,"data":"       |         # B common adjacent to A and C. Order B-A-D-C? Let's think: B adjacent to A and C, opposite vertex is D.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.192667231,"data":"       |         # Order B-A-D-C? Actually sides: BA, BC. So quadrilateral: B-A-D-C (B to A, A to D (parallel to BC), D to C (parallel to BA), C to B)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.192668513,"data":"       |         order = [B, A, D, C]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.192669606,"data":"       |     elif common == 'C':\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.192670662,"data":"       |         D = A + B - C\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.192671747,"data":"       |         order = [C, A, D, B]  # C adjacent to A and B\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.19267316,"data":"       |     else:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.192674222,"data":"       |         raise ValueError\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.192675306,"data":"       |     # compute perimeter as sum of distances between consecutive vertices and back to start\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.19267651,"data":"       |     per = 0\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.192677581,"data":"       |     for i in range(len(order)):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.19267867,"data":"       |         per += order[i].distance(order[(i+1)%len(order)])\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.192679809,"data":"       |     return sp.simplify(per), D, order\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.192680923,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.192681925,"data":"       | for common in ['A','B','C']:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.192682993,"data":"       |     per, D, order = perimeter_given_common(common)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.192684099,"data":"       |     print(common, per, D, order)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4320.192685305,"data":"       | \n"}
