,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4348.021209741,"data":"       | Let’s denote P(t) = (t - a)(t - b)(t - c) = t^3 - s1 t^2 + s2 t - s3, where s1 = a+b+c, s2 = ab+bc+ca, s3 = abc.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4348.021211596,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4348.021212712,"data":"       | We have (a + k)(b + k)(c + k) = ?\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4348.021213921,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4348.021215037,"data":"       | We can express product (a+k)(b+k)(c+k) = ?\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4348.021216266,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4348.021217432,"data":"       | Observe that (a+k)(b+k)(c+k) = (-1)^3 * P(-k) = -P(-k)?? Wait: P(t) = (t-a)(t-b)(t-c). Then P(-k) = (-k - a)(-k - b)(-k - c) = -(a + k) * -(b + k) * -(c + k) = (-1)^3 (a+k)(b+k)(c+k) = - (a+k)(b+k)(c+k). Since (-1)^3 = -1. So (a+k)(b+k)(c+k) = - P(-k).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4348.021219263,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4348.021220348,"data":"       | Thus given values for k=1,2,3: -P(-1)=1 =\u003e P(-1) = -1. Similarly P(-2) = -2, P(-3) = -3.\n"}
