,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4348.021226139,"data":"       | We can determine cubic polynomial P(t) uniquely from its values at three points? Wait cubic has four coefficients; we need 4 constraints. But we also have leading coefficient 1 (monic). So we have 4 constraints: P(t) monic cubic, and values at three points. That's enough to determine P(t). Then compute P(-4).\n"}
