,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4348.021510428,"data":"       | Let’s define function f(x) = (a+x)(b+x)(c+x). This is a cubic polynomial in x: f(x) = (x+a)(x+b)(x+c) = (x^3 + (a+b+c) x^2 + (ab+bc+ca) x + abc). So f(x) is cubic with coefficients expressed in terms of symmetric sums of a,b,c. We are given f(1)=1, f(2)=2, f(3)=3. Need f(4)=?\n"}
