,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4348.021513226,"data":"       | Thus we need to find cubic polynomial f(x) satisfying f(k)=k for k=1,2,3. Then compute f(4). Since f(x) is cubic, we can determine it uniquely given values at 4 points, but we have only 3 points. However we also know leading coefficient is 1 (since product (x+a)(x+b)(x+c) expands to x^3 + ...). Indeed coefficient of x^3 is 1. So we have cubic monic polynomial f(x) with f(1)=1, f(2)=2, f(3)=3. Determine f(4). That seems doable.\n"}
