,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4348.021691643,"data":"       | But we have three conditions for cubic; we need four coefficients. However we have only three equations; but maybe there is additional condition: leading coefficient is 1 (since product expands to t^3 + ...). Indeed coefficient of t^3 is 1 (since each factor contributes t). So we have full determination: P(t) = t^3 + p t^2 + q t + r. Unknown p,q,r. Use P(1)=1, P(2)=2, P(3)=3.\n"}
