,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4348.021769503,"data":"       | But we have products (a + k)(b + k)(c + k) = ? This is equal to P(-k) * (-1)^3? Wait: (a + k)(b + k)(c + k) = ( - ( -a - k) ... not. Actually P(-k) = (-k - a)(-k - b)(-k - c) = -(a + k) * -(b + k) * -(c + k) = (-1)^3 (a + k)(b + k)(c + k) = -(a + k)(b + k)(c + k). Since (-1)^3 = -1. So (a + k)(b + k)(c + k) = - P(-k).\n"}
