,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4348.021793639,"data":"       | Thus we need to find cubic polynomial P(t) = t^3 - S1 t^2 + S2 t - S3 such that P(-1) = -1, P(-2) = -2, P(-3) = -3. That's three conditions, enough to uniquely determine cubic (since cubic has 4 coefficients but leading coefficient is 1 fixed). So we can solve for S1,S2,S3.\n"}
