,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4348.022245199,"data":"       | analysisWe need to find (a+4)(b+4)(c+4) given three equations for (a+1)(b+1)(c+1)=1, (a+2)(b+2)(c+2)=2, (a+3)(b+3)(c+3)=3.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4348.022246523,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4348.022247687,"data":"       | We have three unknowns a,b,c complex numbers, but we have three equations for symmetric expressions (product of shifted variables). The unknowns may be determined up to permutation, but we just need product at shift 4.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4348.022249176,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4348.022250252,"data":"       | Let’s define variables x = a+1, y = b+1, z = c+1. Then a = x-1, b = y-1, c = z-1.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4348.022251489,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4348.022252559,"data":"       | Then we have:\n"}
